@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose CLI entry point + compilation driver for the self-hosting Aria compiler. Parses commands and flags, orchestrates the multi-stage pipeline (lex -> parse -> resolve -> check -> codegen -> build) across single or multi-file projects, reports diagnostics, and dispatches five modes: check / build / run / test / bench.
@depends [lexer, parser, resolver, checker, codegen, diagnostic]

---

@workflow driver
@purpose Raw argv -> exit code
@steps
  1. parse_args validates flags (--format, --target, --runtime, --output, --parallel), maps the first non-flag argument to a command, collects remaining args as file inputs. [src: main.aria:125]
  2. expand_files recursively enumerates .aria files, honours `// test-files:` directives, and sorts by module priority (token/ast/types before consumers). [src: main.aria:754-781]
  3. resolve_stdlib_files scans imports and auto-includes matching stdlib files from lib/ or $ARIA_HOME/lib/. [src: main.aria:458-497]
  4. resolve_local_modules BFS over `use <local_module>` clauses, folding in transitive deps. [src: main.aria:531-576]
  5. Command dispatch runs one of: run_check / run_build / run_run / run_test / run_bench. [src: main.aria:1070-1117]
  6. Diagnostics formatted and printed; exit 0 if no errors (warnings OK), 1 otherwise. [src: main.aria:817-821]

@workflow build_execution
@purpose Source -> binary
@steps
  1. File resolution (as above). [src: main.aria:851-862]
  2. _resolve_and_validate_runtime returns the runtime.c path, or "" on failure. [src: main.aria:609-615]
  3. generate_from_sources runs lex -> parse -> resolve -> check -> lower -> LLVM IR -> clang with runtime. [src: main.aria:867-873]
  4. Output written to --output or derived from raw_files[1]; falls back to a.out. [src: main.aria:619-655]

---

@invariants
  CLI errors exit before command dispatch: if parse_args sets has_error, the driver prints a hint and skips the command handler. [src: main.aria:1076-1078, main.aria:1081-1083]
  Output-path derivation order: explicit --output, then first file's basename/dir, then a.out. [src: main.aria:619-655]
  Module sort places foundational defs (token / ast / types / scope) before their consumers (lexer / parser / checker); insertion sort preserves within-priority order. [src: main.aria:690-736]
  Stdlib vocabulary is a hard-coded list of 12 names (json, http, db, fs, time, log, test, property, crypto, net, os, flag); anything else is local. [src: main.aria:378-381]
  File arrays use 1-indexed convention — index 0 is a sentinel ""; loops start at i := 1. [src: main.aria:45, main.aria:128, main.aria:397, main.aria:536]
  Warnings are printed even on successful runs so the user sees them without having to re-run with --warn. [src: main.aria:817-821, main.aria:873-875, main.aria:902-904]

---

@antipatterns
  Silent runtime-miss: _resolve_and_validate_runtime prints an error but returns "". Callers must check `if rt == ""` — easy to forget. [src: main.aria:609-615, main.aria:861-862]
  Runtime path default "/usr/local/lib/aria" is hard-coded: dev machines without $ARIA_HOME set can fail silently if stdlib isn't at the default. [src: main.aria:483]
  Every run_* subcommand repeats expand_files -> _resolve_local_modules -> _resolve_stdlib_files -> _merge_file_lists. Clear DRY opportunity but any refactor must preserve command-specific file ordering. [src: main.aria:802-811, main.aria:852-860, main.aria:882-890]
  _merge_file_lists dedups with nested-loop basename comparison — O(n^2). Fine for small projects, pathological for larger module graphs. [src: main.aria:579-596]
  No --dry-run / --explain-deps: there's no way to preview the final file set or module resolution without side effects. [src: main.aria:125-176]

