@fn expand_files
@purpose Enumerate all .aria files from the input paths (files + directories), detect `// test-files:` directives, and sort by module priority.
@pre All paths are readable. [src: main.aria:754-782]
@post Returns the sorted file list; a test-files directive short-circuits normal expansion and returns verbatim. [src: main.aria:775-781]
@complexity O(f * d + n log n) — f input paths, d directory depth, n files (insertion sort). [src: main.aria:754-781]
@thread_safety not-safe — Fs effects via _ariaIsDir / _ariaListDir / _ariaReadFile. [src: main.aria:754, main.aria:759-760, main.aria:774]
@antipatterns A test-files directive bypasses module-priority sort, so files listed out-of-order in the directive compile in directive order. [src: main.aria:773-776]

